    "updated_at": "2018-03-15T10:08:06Z",
    "body": "I can see 3 adding overhead, and it's the least valuable part of this, it could be dropped or merged with 3 so that only fatal parse errors throw the JS exception.  1 and 2 should only add measurable overhead if the document was full of syntax errors that cause lots of branching when checking to see if the document opted in to reporting or fatal error handling.  I was hoping this could be done with no overhead for well-formed documents.",
