    "created_at": "2018-03-15T10:48:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-15T10:48:41Z",
    "body": "In practice few folks will be interested in having their servers do both serialization and parsing, at least not in production.  The idea here is to leverage the parsing that's already going to take place in the client, and show errors/warnings where devs are already looking - in the developer console.\r\n\r\nOne way to look at this is to consider https://html5.validator.nu/ a popular server-side implementation.  Presumably anyone using that would be interested in getting a some/most of that validation for \"free\" via the browser.\r\n\r\nClient-side handling could detect more issues than server side could, e.g. problematic plugins, proxies/CDNs, service workers, caches, [browser bugs](https://crbug.com/820163), etc.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
