    "created_at": "2018-03-15T22:55:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-15T22:55:36Z",
    "body": "Is the proposal to log [12.2.2 Parse errors\r\n](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#parse-errors)\r\n\r\n\r\n> Conformance checkers must report at least one parse error condition to the user if one or more parse error conditions exist in the document and must not report parse error conditions if none exist in the document. Conformance checkers may report more than one parse error condition if more than one parse error condition exists in the document.\r\n\r\nto the user, for example at `console` by default? Or is the proposal to send the recognized HTML parse error to an external server? What should occur if the user does not have a `console` to log the parse error; for example Lynx browser?\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
