    "created_at": "2018-03-16T00:23:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-16T00:23:07Z",
    "body": "If the parse error is sent to server, why cannot the data be parsed before the content is delivered? That is, even if a parse error is thrown by a browser and sent to the server, how does the server verify the parse error without re-parsing the HTML?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
