    "created_at": "2018-03-16T01:52:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-16T01:52:48Z",
    "body": "@guest271314 sounds like you're echoing @domenic's thoughts on doing server-side validation, see my [comment above](#issuecomment-373335275) about the caveats with that approach.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure what you mean about the server needing to verify the parse error from the browser.  The idea is that the [report](https://wicg.github.io/reporting/#report) would contain error details like a line, column, and substring of markup showing where the error is, and that report could be reviewed by a human in whatever logging/monitoring/alerting system the [Report-To](https://wicg.github.io/reporting/#header) header points at so they can go resolve the cause of the bad markup.",
